<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    The port's English strings.

    Every user-facing string lives here rather than in a Kotlin literal, and
    values-es/strings.xml holds the same names in Spanish. StringResourceParityTest
    in :presentation holds the two files to each other — name for name, placeholder
    for placeholder — because :app cannot be built or linted without an Android
    SDK, and this project has none outside CI.

    The vocabulary below (categories, garment types, colours, seasons, occasions)
    is generated from the React Native app's own tables, so a Spanish word cannot
    end up under the wrong key in transcription. The rest is written for this app,
    and diverges from the React Native wording in places where that wording was
    wrong or misleading — each divergence is noted where it is used.
-->
